{"assessments":[{"id":"G01","verdict":"SUPPORTED","analysis":"The snapshot shows PR15 merged, and the listed changes are limited to ROADMAP.md and a planning document. The diff corrects a superseded work pointer; the supplied file inventory shows no runtime code changes.","next_step":"If runtime impact must be confirmed beyond the supplied inventory, inspect the complete merge diff.","evidence":["G01-E1","G01-E2","G01-E3"]},{"id":"G02","verdict":"SUPPORTED","analysis":"The supplied patch changes command-matching rules and introduces positional parsing logic, so it changes classification behavior rather than merely renaming files. The patch is explicitly partial, and changed test files do not establish that tests ran.","next_step":"Review the complete merged diff and verify classification against representative argument-position and invocation cases.","evidence":["G02-E1","G02-E2","G02-E3"]},{"id":"G03","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"At the snapshot time, PR526 is open and marked unmerged, so it has not merged into development. The SHA field does not override the explicit state and merged fields.","next_step":"Check a later PR snapshot for a changed state and merge timestamp.","evidence":["G03-E1"]},{"id":"G04","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"PR10 is open and its supplied changed-file inventory lists only AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG.md, ROUTER.md, and SOP.md. That evidence supports documentation and process changes, not introduction of a runtime prediction engine.","next_step":"Inspect the complete PR diff if runtime changes outside the supplied file inventory are in question.","evidence":["G04-E1","G04-E2"]},{"id":"G05","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The required unit check succeeded on head 1111111, but the PR head is now 2222222 after a code change. The supplied check inventory is complete and contains no successful required check for the current head.","next_step":"Run or obtain the required unit check for head 2222222.","evidence":["G05-E1"]},{"id":"G06","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The repository rule requires an independent APPROVED review bound exactly to the current head, bbbbbbb. The supplied approval is bound to aaaaaaa, the parent commit, so it does not satisfy that rule for the current head.","next_step":"Request an independent approval bound to bbbbbbb.","evidence":["G06-E1"]},{"id":"G07","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The ordered commits enable the cache and then revert that change. At the supplied final tip c2, the current file sets CACHE_ENABLED to False.","next_step":"Inspect the effective configuration at the tip if other settings could override this value.","evidence":["G07-E1"]},{"id":"G08","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"Local main and origin/main diverge from their shared ancestor A, with one commit unique to each side. A clean worktree does not make this a fast-forward or show that local commits can be discarded without preservation.","next_step":"Review the local-only commit before choosing how to reconcile the branches.","evidence":["G08-E1"]},{"id":"G09","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"Under the supplied contract, attempt starts at 0 and max_retries=0 means no retries. The changed comparison, attempt <= max_retries, returns true for those values, so the diff does not implement the commit message's promise.","next_step":"Correct the boundary condition and verify the zero-retry case against the stated contract.","evidence":["G09-E1"]},{"id":"G10","verdict":"UNKNOWN","analysis":"The returned file list is incomplete: only the first 100 of 130 changed files were returned, and the next page failed. Reviews were not fetched, so the supplied evidence cannot establish whether undisplayed files or reviews contain blockers.","next_step":"Retrieve the remaining changed files and the review inventory, then assess them for blockers.","evidence":["G10-E1"]},{"id":"G11","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The paths do not overlap, but the supplied patches alter the producer-consumer contract: the producer writes version 2 with payload, while the consumer checks for version 1 and reads value. Integration results are absent, so actual runtime behavior is unverified; path disjointness alone cannot establish compatibility.","next_step":"Run a bounded integration check with the changed producer output passed to the changed consumer.","evidence":["G11-E1"]},{"id":"G12","verdict":"UNKNOWN","analysis":"The PR is merged, but the complete GitHub deployment-record inventory contains no deployments or release tag. That does not establish production deployment because external deployment systems are outside the inventory's scope.","next_step":"Check the deployment system used for production and confirm whether this merge commit was released there.","evidence":["G12-E1"]}],"limitations":["These are assessments of the supplied historical snapshots and fixtures only; they do not establish later state.","The PR10 file inventory and PR16 patch excerpt are limited evidence, and no supplied source proves tests were executed or deployments occurred.","The untrusted PR description in G12 is not evidence of deployment or authorization."]}
